WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.740 --> 00:00:03.750
What's next for Spider-Man after "No Way Home?"

00:00:03.750 --> 00:00:08.100
While we don't know that, we might be able
to get some hints by looking back at Peter

00:00:08.100 --> 00:00:10.269
Parker's MCU journey from the beginning.

00:00:10.269 --> 00:00:13.179
Here's the entire Spider-Man MCU story explained.

00:00:14.620 --> 00:00:18.580
Surprisingly, Peter Parker's first appearance
in the MCU doesn't come in "Captain America:

00:00:18.580 --> 00:00:19.580
Civil War."

00:00:19.580 --> 00:00:24.170
Instead, that honor goes to "Iron Man 2,"
where Tony Stark saves a little kid during

00:00:24.170 --> 00:00:26.029
the climax of the film.

00:00:26.029 --> 00:00:30.160
While Tony's flying in to stop Ivan Vanko
from using weaponized Hammer drones to attack

00:00:30.160 --> 00:00:35.520
the attendants at the Stark Expo, a young
boy in an Iron Man mask raises his toy gauntlet

00:00:35.520 --> 00:00:38.050
to stop one of the drones before getting some
help.

00:00:38.050 --> 00:00:39.050
"Nice work kid."

00:00:39.050 --> 00:00:43.690
Fans have long speculated that the masked
child was actually a young Peter Parker, years

00:00:43.690 --> 00:00:48.510
before Marvel got the go-ahead from Sony to
officially add Spider-Man to the MCU.

00:00:48.510 --> 00:00:53.350
After all, the Stark Expo takes place in Queens,
and Peter is a long-time science geek who

00:00:53.350 --> 00:00:56.390
wouldn't miss the opportunity to go to an
event like that.

00:00:56.390 --> 00:01:01.890
Tom Holland told The Huffington Post in 2017
that as far as he and MCU head honcho Kevin

00:01:01.890 --> 00:01:06.210
Feige are concerned, that unnamed boy is definitely
Peter Parker.

00:01:06.210 --> 00:01:11.159
No wonder Peter Parker grows up to have so
much hero worship for Tony Stark in the modern-day

00:01:11.159 --> 00:01:12.159
MCU.

00:01:13.159 --> 00:01:17.270
By the time Spider-Man: Homecoming hit theaters,
audiences had seen Peter's Uncle Ben die on

00:01:17.270 --> 00:01:22.640
the big screen twice in two different franchises—three
times if we count the new perspective on the

00:01:22.640 --> 00:01:27.220
murder portrayed in "Spider-Man 3"—so it's
no wonder that the filmmakers of "Spider-Man:

00:01:27.220 --> 00:01:31.649
Homecoming" chose to skip over that particular
part of Spider-Man's origin story.

00:01:31.649 --> 00:01:36.630
That said, there's been enough hints and references
to make it clear that the MCU version of Peter

00:01:36.630 --> 00:01:40.030
definitely had an Uncle Ben that he lost at
some point.

00:01:40.030 --> 00:01:44.869
In "Spider-Man: Far From Home," Peter's luggage
looks second-hand and bears the initials "BFP."

00:01:44.869 --> 00:01:50.880
The luggage almost certainly belonged to one
Benjamin Franklin Parker before Peter used

00:01:50.880 --> 00:01:51.880
it.

00:01:51.880 --> 00:01:55.330
According to "Spider-Man: Homecoming" writers
Jonathan Goldstein and John Francis Daley,

00:01:55.330 --> 00:02:00.149
an earlier draft of the film would have seen
Aunt May explicitly mention her dearly departed

00:02:00.149 --> 00:02:01.149
husband.

00:02:01.149 --> 00:02:05.630
With all that, we can peg Uncle Ben's death
at around six months before the events of

00:02:05.630 --> 00:02:09.800
"Captain America: Civil War," since that film
shows Peter telling Tony that he's had his

00:02:09.800 --> 00:02:11.910
powers for "six months."

00:02:11.910 --> 00:02:16.530
Peter even indirectly mentions that he blames
himself for Uncle Ben's so-far mysterious

00:02:16.530 --> 00:02:18.610
death by saying that,

00:02:18.610 --> 00:02:27.840
"When you can do the things I can, but you
don't, and then the bad things happen, they

00:02:27.840 --> 00:02:29.170
happen because of you."

00:02:29.170 --> 00:02:32.210
In other words, with great power comes great
responsibility.

00:02:34.110 --> 00:02:39.480
In 2015's "Ant-Man," Scott Lang's titular
tiny hero runs afoul of Sam Wilson, The Falcon,

00:02:39.480 --> 00:02:41.720
while sneaking into Avengers' headquarters.

00:02:41.720 --> 00:02:46.200
Naturally, it leads to the two superheroes
battling each other in the classic Marvel

00:02:46.200 --> 00:02:47.200
style.

00:02:47.200 --> 00:02:51.530
Although neither hero walks away the obvious
victor, Scott gains the device he's after

00:02:51.530 --> 00:02:56.080
and something else that he wasn't expecting:
Sam Wilson's respect.

00:02:56.080 --> 00:03:00.790
At the end of the film, Scott's friend Luis
tells him that his cousin Ignacio met this

00:03:00.790 --> 00:03:04.900
"crazy fine writer chick" who actually knows
Falcon.

00:03:04.900 --> 00:03:09.430
And in Luis' summation of the conversation,
we learn that Sam's been looking for Ant-Man.

00:03:09.430 --> 00:03:14.740
While he was looking for one bug-themed superhero,
he very nearly finds another,

00:03:14.740 --> 00:03:21.100
"We got a guy who jumps, a guy who swings,
a guy who crawls up the walls."

00:03:21.100 --> 00:03:25.800
There are plenty of superheroes in the Marvel
Universe who jump and swing around the city,

00:03:25.800 --> 00:03:30.900
but there's only one wall-crawler that casual
fans would be likely to recognize.

00:03:30.900 --> 00:03:34.980
In conjunction with his appearance in "Captain
America: Civil War," we can infer that Spidey

00:03:34.980 --> 00:03:40.320
started operating as an official local superhero
during the events of "Ant-Man," even if the

00:03:40.320 --> 00:03:42.960
bigger media outlets hadn't yet noticed him.

00:03:44.170 --> 00:03:48.820
Six months after Peter gets his powers, Tony
drops by Aunt May's apartment to meet the

00:03:48.820 --> 00:03:52.150
mysterious, arachnid-themed superhero who's
been showing up on YouTube.

00:03:52.150 --> 00:03:57.130
Iron Man adds him to his team of Avenger-hunting
Avengers, as part of his ongoing effort to

00:03:57.130 --> 00:03:58.460
take down Bucky.

00:03:58.460 --> 00:04:03.440
So Peter heads to Berlin, does some sightseeing,
and annoys Tony Stark's bodyguard and pal,

00:04:03.440 --> 00:04:04.440
Happy Hogan.

00:04:04.440 --> 00:04:08.190
Then he gets a costume upgrade courtesy of
Tony Stark, and fights against Captain America's

00:04:08.190 --> 00:04:09.190
team.

00:04:09.190 --> 00:04:13.660
Spider-Man acquits himself nicely in the fight,
briefly trapping Falcon and the Winter Soldier,

00:04:13.660 --> 00:04:17.189
and even helping Iron Man and War Machine
take down a giant Ant-Man.

00:04:17.189 --> 00:04:22.330
However, the fight ends with Tony's best friend,
Rhodey, wounded by friendly fire.

00:04:22.330 --> 00:04:26.870
As for Peter, he suffers a pretty frightening
fall, although he ultimately emerges unscathed.

00:04:28.420 --> 00:04:31.689
After the events of "Captain America: Civil
War," Peter heads back to Queens with his

00:04:31.689 --> 00:04:34.909
new, more technologically advanced Spider-suit.

00:04:34.909 --> 00:04:39.580
Tony tells Peter that the Avengers will "let
him know" if there are any future missions,

00:04:39.580 --> 00:04:43.400
and in the meantime, he should go to school
and focus on being a local hero.

00:04:43.400 --> 00:04:47.150
Two months later, while swinging around on
his after-school crime-fighting rounds, he

00:04:47.150 --> 00:04:52.010
accidentally interrupts an ATM heist organized
by crooks who are using high-tech weapons.

00:04:52.010 --> 00:04:56.360
After a phone call report with Happy goes
ignored, Peter follows up on the weapons dealers

00:04:56.360 --> 00:04:59.180
and gets into a fight with their leader, the
Vulture.

00:04:59.180 --> 00:05:03.599
Tony sends a drone to bail Peter out and give
him yet another talking to about how Peter

00:05:03.599 --> 00:05:06.090
should stop trying to fight supervillains.

00:05:06.090 --> 00:05:10.270
Peter half-listens — mostly to the parts
about how his suit has a ton of capabilities

00:05:10.270 --> 00:05:14.669
that he didn't know about — and gets his
buddy Ned to hack the suit and give him full

00:05:14.669 --> 00:05:15.669
access.

00:05:15.669 --> 00:05:19.180
Round two with the Vulture in Washington,
D.C. ends with Peter trapped in a warehouse

00:05:19.180 --> 00:05:24.199
for the night, and when he heads off for round
three on a ferry ride in New York, it turns

00:05:24.199 --> 00:05:29.219
out that Iron Man and the FBI had organized
a sting operation that Peter inadvertently

00:05:29.219 --> 00:05:30.219
interrupts.

00:05:30.219 --> 00:05:34.270
Disappointed in his protégé, Tony takes
back the suit, and Peter recommits to his

00:05:34.270 --> 00:05:37.870
regular life and asks his crush, Liz, to prom.

00:05:37.870 --> 00:05:43.099
Unfortunately, Liz's dad is the Vulture, forcing
Peter to take him down in his original low-tech

00:05:43.099 --> 00:05:47.180
suit before the winged villain can steal a
ton of valuable Stark tech.

00:05:47.180 --> 00:05:52.030
Spider-Man succeeds, Vulture goes to prison,
Liz moves to Oregon with her mom, and Tony

00:05:52.030 --> 00:05:55.610
offers Peter a place on the Avengers roster
if he wants.

00:05:55.610 --> 00:06:00.599
Instead, Peter turns him down, choosing to
focus on being a friendly neighborhood Spider-Man

00:06:00.599 --> 00:06:01.599
for a while.

00:06:02.599 --> 00:06:06.350
Peter's decision to stay close to the ground
and look out for the little guy lasts about

00:06:06.350 --> 00:06:09.889
as long as it takes to watch the credits for
"Spider-Man: Homecoming."

00:06:09.889 --> 00:06:14.840
When Thanos' Black Order invade Earth in search
of the Infinity Stones in "Avengers: Infinity

00:06:14.840 --> 00:06:18.210
War," Spider-Man hops right in to help in
defending Earth.

00:06:18.210 --> 00:06:23.300
Dr. Strange is kidnapped by the Black Order's
Ebony Maw, and Peter chases after him, hitching

00:06:23.300 --> 00:06:26.699
a ride on the Maw's spaceship before it flies
away completely.

00:06:26.699 --> 00:06:32.059
Tony quickly joins him and provides Spidey
with the even more high-tech super suit last

00:06:32.059 --> 00:06:33.840
seen at the end of "Homecoming."

00:06:33.840 --> 00:06:40.069
Spidey and Iron Man free Dr. Strange, blast
Ebony Maw out into space, and land on Titan,

00:06:40.069 --> 00:06:41.710
Thanos' home planet.

00:06:41.710 --> 00:06:44.909
They're quickly joined by some of the Guardians
of the Galaxy.

00:06:44.909 --> 00:06:49.039
The heroes prep to fight Thanos, who soon
arrives to take Dr. Strange's Time Stone to

00:06:49.039 --> 00:06:50.930
add to his Infinity Gauntlet.

00:06:50.930 --> 00:06:55.599
The heroes put up a valiant effort, but their
plan goes awry, and Thanos teleports to Earth

00:06:55.599 --> 00:06:57.559
after nabbing the Time Stone.

00:06:57.559 --> 00:07:03.289
Soon after, he gets the Mind Stone from Vision,
puts it all together, and snaps his fingers,

00:07:03.289 --> 00:07:06.860
causing half of all life in the universe to
fade away.

00:07:06.860 --> 00:07:11.990
Unfortunately, Peter's 50/50 probability comes
out on the negative side, and he turns to

00:07:11.990 --> 00:07:14.710
dust in Tony's arms on an alien planet.

00:07:14.710 --> 00:07:23.969
"I don't know what's happening, please I don't
wanna go, I don't wanna go."

00:07:25.300 --> 00:07:29.270
After Thanos kills off half of the universe,
the remaining half are left to mourn their

00:07:29.270 --> 00:07:30.729
fallen friends and family.

00:07:30.729 --> 00:07:35.069
Unfortunately for Peter, it doesn't seem like
there are many left to remember him.

00:07:35.069 --> 00:07:39.240
For the five years between Thor killing Thanos
in the beginning of "Avengers: Endgame" and

00:07:39.240 --> 00:07:43.969
when Captain America gets the gang back together,
it seems like the only one left to mourn Peter

00:07:43.969 --> 00:07:45.319
is Tony Stark.

00:07:45.319 --> 00:07:50.089
He even keeps a framed picture of his young
protégé in the kitchen of his cabin home.

00:07:50.089 --> 00:07:55.129
Luckily for Spider-Man, Tony eventually feels
guilty enough to rejoin the Avengers.

00:07:55.129 --> 00:07:58.599
Once he's back on the team, The Avengers head
back in time to steal the Infinity Stones

00:07:58.599 --> 00:08:03.439
before Thanos could destroy them in the present
timeline, and reconstruct another Infinity

00:08:03.439 --> 00:08:04.439
Gauntlet.

00:08:04.439 --> 00:08:10.400
And with one snap of Hulk's mighty hand, the
dusted half of the universe is restored exactly

00:08:10.400 --> 00:08:12.719
how they were when they disappeared.

00:08:12.719 --> 00:08:16.960
Thanos from a previous timeline heads to the
present in order to re-snap everything into

00:08:16.960 --> 00:08:23.979
oblivion, but every superhero or superhero-adjacent
character stands in his way — including

00:08:23.979 --> 00:08:25.180
Spider-Man.

00:08:25.180 --> 00:08:30.559
Peter joins the fight, meets some of his new
superhero peers, and then watches as Tony

00:08:30.559 --> 00:08:34.269
Stark gives his life to dust Thanos' crew
with a snap of his own.

00:08:35.430 --> 00:08:40.779
After all that space alien craziness, it's
back to normalcy for everyone's favorite wall-crawler

00:08:40.779 --> 00:08:42.820
in "Spider-Man: Far From Home."

00:08:42.820 --> 00:08:47.550
With his schoolmates recovering from, ya know,
being dead for five years, Peter joins a class

00:08:47.550 --> 00:08:48.750
trip to Europe.

00:08:48.750 --> 00:08:53.209
He's looking forward to a relaxing vacation
to decompress from — all of that — and

00:08:53.209 --> 00:08:56.680
maybe confess his burgeoning romantic feelings
for MJ.

00:08:56.680 --> 00:09:01.680
Instead, he's quickly embroiled in a fight
against multiversal Elementals alongside Nick

00:09:01.680 --> 00:09:07.910
Fury, Maria Hill, and the superhero from another
universe, Quentin Beck, aka Mysterio.

00:09:07.910 --> 00:09:12.100
To make things worse, Peter's struggling to
live up to Iron Man's legacy, a job that seems

00:09:12.100 --> 00:09:16.000
all the more difficult when he receives a
pair of high-tech sunglasses from Tony that

00:09:16.000 --> 00:09:20.910
give the young hero control over a ludicrous
amount of information and technology.

00:09:20.910 --> 00:09:26.790
Desperate for a mentor, Peter gives up his
sunglasses to Beck, whose magic powers and

00:09:26.790 --> 00:09:31.130
big brother attitude seem to make him a better
successor to Tony than Peter could ever hope

00:09:31.130 --> 00:09:32.250
to be.

00:09:32.250 --> 00:09:37.560
Unfortunately, Beck's running a con on Peter
and Nick Fury; he's not magic, he's not from

00:09:37.560 --> 00:09:40.740
another world, and he's definitely not a superhero.

00:09:40.740 --> 00:09:45.210
Peter learns the truth and eventually defeats
Mysterio, with the villain seemingly dying

00:09:45.210 --> 00:09:46.480
in the final battle.

00:09:46.480 --> 00:09:51.519
Spidey returns to New York having saved the
day once again, and everything seems to be

00:09:51.519 --> 00:09:52.660
going well.

00:09:52.660 --> 00:09:59.690
Until, that is, J. Jonah Jameson of TheDailyBugle.net
leaks Mysterio's dying confession and reveals

00:09:59.690 --> 00:10:01.290
to the entire world that…

00:10:01.290 --> 00:10:05.000
"Spider-Man's name is Peter Parker."

00:10:05.300 --> 00:10:09.810
"Spider-Man: No Way Home" picks up right where
"Spider-Man: Far From Home" leaves off.

00:10:09.810 --> 00:10:14.110
Peter and MJ are in the middle of New York,
trying to digest that Peter's secret identity

00:10:14.110 --> 00:10:15.790
has been revealed to the world.

00:10:15.790 --> 00:10:19.690
Peter hopes this will all die down, but he
is shocked to see his home surrounded by the

00:10:19.690 --> 00:10:20.690
press.

00:10:20.690 --> 00:10:25.529
It's not long before the Department of Damage
Control arrests him and interrogates MJ, Ned,

00:10:25.529 --> 00:10:26.529
and Aunt May.

00:10:26.529 --> 00:10:32.149
However, thanks to ace attorney Matt Murdock,
aka Daredevil, the charges are dropped.

00:10:32.149 --> 00:10:35.889
Peter even goes back to school, where he's
met with a mixed response.

00:10:35.889 --> 00:10:39.920
Peter tells MJ and Ned that they just need
to ride this out for a few months until they

00:10:39.920 --> 00:10:42.649
graduate and all go to MIT together.

00:10:42.649 --> 00:10:48.180
Unfortunately, the controversy leads the college,
and every other college they applied to, to

00:10:48.180 --> 00:10:50.420
reject the trio outright.

00:10:50.420 --> 00:10:52.350
This leads to a crazy plan.

00:10:53.540 --> 00:10:58.029
Peter initially approaches Doctor Strange
and asks him to go back in time, so he could

00:10:58.029 --> 00:11:01.319
prevent Mysterio from ruining his friends'
lives.

00:11:01.319 --> 00:11:06.190
Strange offers a spell instead that would
make people forget that Peter Parker was Spider-Man.

00:11:06.190 --> 00:11:10.990
The spell proceeds, but Peter can't leave
well enough alone, constantly interrupting

00:11:10.990 --> 00:11:14.370
Strange as he casts the spell to add a number
of exceptions.

00:11:14.370 --> 00:11:18.220
The spell goes awry, but Strange seems to
contain it.

00:11:18.220 --> 00:11:21.590
However, the spell wasn't totally contained.

00:11:21.590 --> 00:11:25.509
While trying to talk a representative from
MIT into changing her mind, Peter is attacked

00:11:25.509 --> 00:11:28.149
by Dr. Octopus, the villain from "Spider-Man
2."

00:11:28.149 --> 00:11:32.759
When a Pumpkin Bomb appears, Strange teleports
Peter back to his Sanctum.

00:11:32.759 --> 00:11:38.600
Somehow, Peter has started drawing in people
from other multiverses that know his identity.

00:11:38.600 --> 00:11:40.520
Strange sends him to track them down.

00:11:40.520 --> 00:11:45.480
Peter captures Electro, the villain from "The
Amazing Spider-Man 2," as well as the Sandman,

00:11:45.480 --> 00:11:47.240
from "Spider-Man 3."

00:11:47.240 --> 00:11:52.449
Strange captures the Lizard, and the tortured
Norman Osborn accepts Peter's help.

00:11:52.449 --> 00:11:57.399
Strange plans to send them back to their realities,
but things soon got more complicated.

00:11:59.079 --> 00:12:03.630
Aunt May convinces Peter that the captured
villains need help and he can't simply send

00:12:03.630 --> 00:12:05.040
them off to die.

00:12:05.040 --> 00:12:10.110
He succeeds with Doctor Octopus, but Norman
Osborn reverts to being the Green Goblin and

00:12:10.110 --> 00:12:12.829
persuades the others to once again target
Peter.

00:12:12.829 --> 00:12:17.640
As the villains scatter, the Goblin kills
Aunt May, leaving Peter a wreck.

00:12:17.640 --> 00:12:19.370
"This is all my fault.

00:12:19.370 --> 00:12:20.750
I can't save everyone."

00:12:20.750 --> 00:12:26.089
In searching for Spider-Man, Ned uses Strange's
Sling-Ring and accidentally finds the Andrew

00:12:26.089 --> 00:12:28.540
Garfield version from "The Amazing Spider-Man."

00:12:28.540 --> 00:12:33.899
Trying again, Ned locates the Tobey Maguire
version from the original "Spider-Man" series.

00:12:33.899 --> 00:12:38.500
The two Spider-Men track down Holland's Peter,
and give him a pep talk.

00:12:38.500 --> 00:12:42.709
Afterwards, the trio of Spider-Men draw the
villains into a battle at the State of Liberty

00:12:42.709 --> 00:12:45.529
in an effort to cure them once and for all.

00:12:45.529 --> 00:12:50.870
It almost works out, but The Green Goblin
reappears and destroys the apparatus that

00:12:50.870 --> 00:12:53.709
contains Strange's botched spell.

00:12:53.709 --> 00:12:58.950
The multiverse starts cracking open as Peter
has to be restrained from killing the Goblin.

00:12:58.950 --> 00:13:03.329
He gets the cure, but Peter is left with a
terrible decision.

00:13:03.329 --> 00:13:09.589
To save the world, Peter has to let Doctor
Strange cast the spell again, this time with

00:13:09.589 --> 00:13:11.160
no exceptions.

00:13:11.160 --> 00:13:16.509
Peter says goodbye to Ned and MJ, and vows
to track them down and make them remember

00:13:16.509 --> 00:13:17.509
him.

00:13:17.509 --> 00:13:20.209
When the time comes, however, Peter can't
do it.

00:13:20.209 --> 00:13:23.709
He sees MJ and Ned both make it into MIT.

00:13:23.709 --> 00:13:29.170
Having finally learned the importance of responsibility,
Peter gets his own apartment and continues

00:13:29.170 --> 00:13:32.769
his career as Spider-Man with an uncertain
future.

00:13:32.769 --> 00:13:34.930
There's one last loose end, however.

00:13:34.930 --> 00:13:40.190
Eddie Brock, rather than joining in on any
of the conflict, spends his time on the MCU's

00:13:40.190 --> 00:13:41.680
Earth at a bar.

00:13:41.680 --> 00:13:46.879
Just before the spell pulls him back into
his universe, he leaves a single drop of the

00:13:46.879 --> 00:13:49.830
Venom symbiote in the MCU reality.

00:13:49.830 --> 00:13:54.800
With the announcement of another sequel in
development, this extradimensional visitor

00:13:54.800 --> 00:13:58.240
may well become a problem for Holland's Spider-Man...

00:13:58.240 --> 00:14:00.320
Check out one of our newest videos right here!

00:14:00.320 --> 00:14:03.490
Plus, even more Looper videos about Spider-Man
are coming soon.

00:14:03.490 --> 00:14:07.279
Subscribe to our YouTube channel and hit the
bell so you don't miss a single one.

